@startuml
title P1 History and Receipt Lifecycle

hide empty description

state "Client-visible history item" as History {
  [*] --> processing
  processing --> ready : media normalized
  processing --> error : probe/transcode failed
  ready --> playing : started on target set
  ready --> partial : mixed target outcome
  ready --> error : no playable targets\nor cancelled failure
  playing --> played : all started targets ended
  playing --> partial : some targets failed or missed
  partial --> [*]
  played --> [*]
  error --> [*]
}

state "Per-target receipt detail" as Receipt {
  [*] --> accepted
  accepted --> preparing
  preparing --> ready
  ready --> scheduled
  scheduled --> playing
  playing --> played

  accepted --> missed_offline
  accepted --> missed_dnd
  accepted --> missed_not_ready
  accepted --> blocked
  accepted --> failed
}

History --> Receipt : aggregates exact reasons

state "Explicit history action" as Action {
  [*] --> reauthorize
  reauthorize --> rejected : actor/item/action changed
  reauthorize --> delegated : current action allowed
  delegated --> replayed : new accepted_at +\nfresh target snapshot
  delegated --> deleted : media tombstone +\ncancellation outbox
  delegated --> reported : moderation evidence + audit
  delegated --> blocked : canonical actor/orbit block
  replayed --> idempotent_result : same actor/key/request
  deleted --> idempotent_result : repeated owner delete
  reported --> idempotent_result : same reporter/media
  blocked --> idempotent_result : policy request replay
  rejected --> [*]
  idempotent_result --> [*]
}

History --> Action : hints only; command reauthorizes

note bottom of Action
  Presence surfaces may show online/offline, output state,
  playback state, required capability support, DND, and block.
  They must never expose microphone state or local process names.
  Replay is a new explicit delivery, never receipt resurrection or inbox
  autoplay. Deleted/expired media cannot be revived. Manual app/hardware
  verification remains in the dedicated testing epic.
end note

@enduml
